  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this shows",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Read from the **gateway's own spend log** (`LiteLLM_SpendLogs` in Postgres), not from the inference engine. That is deliberate: this stack runs vLLM *or* llama.cpp depending on whether throughput or context matters more, and an engine-specific dashboard goes blank the moment you switch. vLLM's Prometheus metrics also carry no user dimension — they answer *how many tokens*, never *whose*.\n\nEvery request through `gateway.<domain>` lands here, from the API and the web UI alike. GPU panels come from the `nvidia-smi` exporter, which reports whichever engine holds the card.\n\nvLLM-native panels are in the collapsed row at the bottom. They light up when vLLM is the running engine and stay empty otherwise — that is expected, not a fault."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Requests",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "litellm-db"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "litellm-db"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT count(*) AS \"Requests\" FROM \"LiteLLM_SpendLogs\" WHERE $__timeFilter(\"startTime\")"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
